<?php
/**
 * Hub Market — "You qualify for free shipping" in the cart summary.
 *
 * This store really does offer it: an active cart price rule grants free
 * shipping over a subtotal threshold (base_subtotal >= 50, no end date, all
 * customer groups, website 1). The freeshipping CARRIER is switched off, so the
 * promise lives entirely in that rule.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * WHY THIS ASKS THE QUOTE AND NOT THE RULE
 *
 * The obvious build is a view model that reads the rule, finds the threshold and
 * renders "Spend X more for free shipping" — the useful half of the feature. I
 * wrote it. It cannot ship without `setup:di:compile`.
 *
 * This install runs production mode with compiled DI (generated/metadata
 * present, 6587 generated classes), so the ObjectManager uses the compiled
 * factory. A class added since the last compile has no definition, resolving an
 * <argument xsi:type="object"> to it throws, and Magento drops the whole block
 * SILENTLY — no exception logged, no output, nothing to notice. The already
 * compiled ProductSavings view model on the PDP uses the same mechanism and
 * works, which is what isolated it.
 *
 * Compiling means taking the storefront down on a two core box, so the feature
 * is built the way that needs no new class: the quote already knows whether free
 * shipping was granted, whatever granted it — rule, coupon or carrier. That is
 * also exactly what the reference draws, which shows only the earned state.
 *
 * MagentoEgypt\CheckoutExtend\ViewModel\FreeShipping is kept for the day a
 * compile happens; swapping to it is a one line layout change.
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * @var \Magento\Checkout\Block\Cart $block
 * @var \Magento\Framework\Escaper $escaper
 */
/*
 * THE TEST IS THE CHARGE, NOT THE FLAG.
 *
 * The first version asked the address for getFreeShipping(). On this install
 * that returns TRUE while the shopper is still charged: rule 2 matches at
 * subtotal >= 50 and sets the flag, but the Flat Rate carrier ignores it
 * because carriers/flatrate/free_shipping_enable is unset, so a 3 x EGP 34 cart
 * shows "You qualify for free shipping" directly above "Shipping EGP 15".
 * Verified by building a quote server side: flag true, shipping amount 15,
 * applied rule 2.
 *
 * Reading the actual shipping amount cannot contradict the total printed beside
 * it. It also means this line switches itself on the moment the carrier config
 * is corrected, with no code change.
 */
$hmQualified = false;
try {
    $hmQuote = $block->getQuote();
    if ($hmQuote && $hmQuote->getItemsCount() && !$hmQuote->isVirtual()) {
        $hmAddress = $hmQuote->getShippingAddress();
        $hmQualified = $hmAddress
            && $hmAddress->getShippingMethod()
            && (float) $hmAddress->getShippingAmount() === 0.0
            && (float) $hmQuote->getBaseSubtotal() > 0;
    }
} catch (\Throwable $e) {
    //  A notice is decoration; it must never take the cart page down.
    $hmQualified = false;
}

if (!$hmQualified) {
    return;
}
?>
<p class="hm-cart__freeship hm-cart__freeship--won">
    <svg class="hm-icon hm-icon--sm" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#hm-check"/></svg>
    <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('You qualify for free shipping')) ?>
</p>
